exports[`compileBundle on the shop project the neutral layer is a snapshot on the shop project: neutral 1`] = `
[
  {
    "content": 
"# Neutral layer

The change described without any programming language, for a team that does not use the nestjs-ts target.

- \`model.json\`: new and extended entities, value objects, events, ports and use-cases; state transitions (an empty list means the Delta declares none); every invariant with its stable id, text and given/when/then examples; the acceptance criteria of the proposal, if there is one.
- \`briefs/\`: one brief per item, in wave order.

Text quoted from the change request is escaped; only the surrounding framework text is guaranteed to contain no TypeScript.

This layer has no \`done\` certification: only the nestjs-ts target layer is certified, so a team implementing from here owns its own verification.
"
,
    "path": "neutral/README.md",
  },
  {
    "content": 
"# Brief: entity:Order

Wave 1, domain layer. Finish every item of an earlier wave first.

## Job

Extend the existing entity Order with the members listed in model.json and nothing else.
States: open, paid
Operations: refund (each has its own brief)

## Business rules and examples

### invariant:Order/paid-once

Refunds a paid order.

Example 1
- Given: Refunds a paid order.
- When: Refunds a paid order.
- Then: Refunds a paid order.

## Rules

- model.json, one folder up, is the full specification; this brief is the slice for one item.
- Use your own language, layout and test tools. Keep invariant ids and business text exactly as written.
- This layer has no \`done\` certification: only the nestjs-ts target layer is certified, so a team implementing from here owns its own verification.
"
,
    "path": "neutral/briefs/entity-Order.md",
  },
  {
    "content": 
"# Brief: method:Order.pay

Wave 2, domain layer. Finish every item of an earlier wave first.

## Job

Implement the element method:Order.pay as described in model.json.

## Rules

- model.json, one folder up, is the full specification; this brief is the slice for one item.
- Use your own language, layout and test tools. Keep invariant ids and business text exactly as written.
- This layer has no \`done\` certification: only the nestjs-ts target layer is certified, so a team implementing from here owns its own verification.
"
,
    "path": "neutral/briefs/method-Order-pay.md",
  },
  {
    "content": 
"# Brief: method:Order.refund

Wave 2, domain layer. Finish every item of an earlier wave first.

## Job

Implement the operation refund of Order.

Refunds a paid order.

Inputs:
- reason (optional text)
Returns: nothing
State change: from paid to open
Announces events: OrderRefunded

## Business rules and examples

### invariant:Order/refund-needs-paid

Refunds a paid order.

Example 1
- Given: g
- When: w
- Then: t

## Rules

- model.json, one folder up, is the full specification; this brief is the slice for one item.
- Use your own language, layout and test tools. Keep invariant ids and business text exactly as written.
- This layer has no \`done\` certification: only the nestjs-ts target layer is certified, so a team implementing from here owns its own verification.
"
,
    "path": "neutral/briefs/method-Order-refund.md",
  },
  {
    "content": 
"# Brief: usecase:pay_order

Wave 3, application layer. Finish every item of an earlier wave first.

## Job

Extend the existing use-case pay_order with what is listed here.
Calls operations: Order.refund
Announces events: OrderRefunded

## Rules

- model.json, one folder up, is the full specification; this brief is the slice for one item.
- Use your own language, layout and test tools. Keep invariant ids and business text exactly as written.
- This layer has no \`done\` certification: only the nestjs-ts target layer is certified, so a team implementing from here owns its own verification.
"
,
    "path": "neutral/briefs/usecase-pay_order.md",
  },
  {
    "content": 
"{
  "module": "shop",
  "certification": "This layer has no \`done\` certification: only the nestjs-ts target layer is certified, so a team implementing from here owns its own verification.",
  "entities": [
    {
      "name": "Order",
      "existing": true,
      "description": null,
      "states": [
        "open",
        "paid"
      ],
      "invariants": [
        "invariant:Order/paid-once"
      ],
      "methods": [
        {
          "name": "refund",
          "description": "Refunds a paid order.",
          "static": false,
          "inputs": [
            {
              "name": "reason",
              "type": "text",
              "optional": true
            }
          ],
          "returns": "nothing",
          "emits": [
            "OrderRefunded"
          ],
